# TypeScript quality — mandatory for agents

## Primary references

- **[`docs/code-quality.md`](../../docs/code-quality.md)** — TypeScript summary, per-app baselines, DTO alignment table, `any` hotspots.
- **[`.agents/skills/typescript-quality/SKILL.md`](../../.agents/skills/typescript-quality/SKILL.md)** — Monorepo workflow; load on every TS/JS task.
- **`typescript-best-practices`** — `c:\Users\saada\.claude\skills\typescript-best-practices\SKILL.md` (discriminated unions, Zod, branded types).
- **[`.agents/skills/fallow/SKILL.md`](../../.agents/skills/fallow/SKILL.md)** — `unused-types`, semantic dupes (type drift signal).

Works together with [`.cursor/rules/code-quality.mdc`](./code-quality.mdc) and [`.cursor/rules/documentation-updates.mdc`](./documentation-updates.mdc).

## When this applies

Same scope as `code-quality.mdc`: any change to `.ts`, `.tsx`, `.js`, `.jsx`, or TS config in `BookMyBarber-bk/`, `BookMyBarber-admin/`, `BookMyBarber-App/`.

## Before coding (read)

1. **`docs/code-quality.md`** — TypeScript section for the workspace you touch.
2. Load **`typescript-best-practices`** + **typescript-quality** skills.
3. For API work: backend route/service type is canonical; client types in `src/lib/` must stay aligned.

## During implementation

- **No new `any`** in backend (currently clean). Avoid new `any` in clients; replace when editing a function.
- **Backend POST/PATCH** — prefer Zod schema + `z.infer` for request bodies (trust boundaries).
- **Clients** — typed `api.get/post<…>` or explicit response interfaces; no `@supabase/supabase-js` types.
- **Roles / status** — `as const` arrays + union types; exhaustive `switch` with `never` default.
- **Fallow dupes** on identical interfaces — sync client mirror to backend DTO or extract shared backend `types.ts` and document client subset.

## Analyze (required with Fallow)

From monorepo root, for **each affected package**:

```bash
cd BookMyBarber-bk && npx tsc --noEmit 2>/dev/null || true
cd BookMyBarber-admin && npx tsc --noEmit 2>/dev/null || true
cd BookMyBarber-App && npx tsc --noEmit 2>/dev/null || true

FALLOW_AGENT_SOURCE=cursor npx fallow dead-code --format json --quiet --unused-types --workspace <workspace> 2>/dev/null || true
```

Plus the standard Fallow commands in `code-quality.mdc`.

## After every change (update docs)

1. Re-run `tsc --noEmit` + Fallow (including `--unused-types`) for touched workspaces.
2. **Update `docs/code-quality.md`** — bump **Last report**; refresh TypeScript table (`tsc`, `any` count, unused types) or add session note.
3. **Update `docs/PROJECT_PROGRESS.md`** when type/API contracts changed.

## Do not

- Use `@ts-ignore` / `@ts-expect-error` to merge.
- Import backend source into clients.
- Skip type checks on “small” edits.
- Treat Fallow as a substitute for `tsc` (Fallow explicitly does not type-check).
